      "title": "Musk distances from MAGA after Republican losses; Trump calls him a friend",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/world-news/musk-distances-from-maga-after-republican-losses-trump-calls-him-a-friend-126112000024_1.html",
      "description": "Elon Musk was in the front row at Donald Trump's second inauguration and has spent hundreds of millions of dollars trying to help the Republican president and his \"Make America Great Again\" allies win elections.\nNow, after Republicans' midterm thrashing by Democrats, the world's richest man insists he's not a MAGA acolyte after all and feels \"pretty foolish\" for spending so much money on the cause.\nIt's the latest example of billionaire tech executives shifting their stances as Democrats prepare to take control of Congress and many more US statehouses in January after they spent months promising a regulatory and oversight crackdown on artificial intelligence firms, their data centre expansion and their interactions with the Trump administration.\n\"I mean, I'm not MAGA,\" Musk told The New York Times on Wednesday during the newspaper's DealBook Summit.\n\"I'm not sure what MAGA means,\" added the Tesla and SpaceX CEO, who once sported a black MAGA hat in the Oval Office and coined the \"D",
